    "created_at": "2021-04-06T23:59:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-04-06T23:59:53Z",
    "body": "See the following public-webapps threads:\r\n- https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-webapps/2011OctDec/0663.html\r\n- https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-webapps/2012AprJun/0022.html\r\n- https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-webapps/2012AprJun/0273.html\r\n\r\nThis wasn't really prevented / motivated by the compatibility concern. It was because `innerHTML` on `template` and `ShadowRoot` was conceptualized as a way to be able to support setter. With `DocumentFragment` which is not `ShadowRoot`, we don't know the context element so we need to decide which parsing mode to use. It would be indeed weird & controversial to introduce `innerHTML` that only supports getting but not setting since that could be a compatibility concern especially if we decide to throw an exception in the setter.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
