    "created_at": "2021-05-18T05:48:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-05-18T05:48:33Z",
    "body": "> So I'll leave this open for a bit to see if there is a compelling counterargument, but I'm inclined to close this given the above.\r\n\r\nIt might be a separate issue, but could we get a way to serialize a whole document? (other than `XMLSerializer` which forces XHTML even if the document is HTML).\r\n\r\nSerializing a `document` doesn't suffer from the context-specific deserialization/serialization issue so it should be fine to expose.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
