    "updated_at": "2021-05-18T10:31:56Z",
    "body": "@LeaVerou the serialization doesn't depend on the context, but the parsing of it does. Given that mismatch, offering context-free serialization (i.e., `documentFragmentInstance.something` rather than `someElement.innerHTML`) will likely lead to subtle problems in practice. (As you know there's no way we can annotate the string and say that it can be only be handed to `innerHTML` successfully when used on a tr element or some such.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
